-- CONTROL: the OTHER import order (ifacea's line first, ifaceb's second), with
-- Blob implementing the interface `mth` actually resolves to (IB) this time.  A
-- bare order-swap ALONE (same impl, same namedFrom as main.mdk) lands on the
-- issue's matrix "correct-reject" cell (exit 1), which this harness cannot
-- express as a green control -- control: always requires exit 0.  So this
-- control pairs the flipped order with a matching impl: mth still resolves to
-- IB, same as main.mdk, and Blob now genuinely implements IB, which is what this
-- order happens to check against.  Checked-against and actually-used now agree
-- for the RIGHT reason, and the program is honestly valid.  It must stay green
-- and print `2` -- if it breaks, module loading / interface resolution broke,
-- not #1092.
import ifacea.{IA}
import ifaceb.{IB, mth}

public export data Blob = Blob
export impl IB Blob where
  mth b = 2

main = println (mth Blob)
